in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @epistemologic/property/content_addressed
in @epistemologic/property/laws/monoidal

# @mirror/store/spectral_uuid — the graph-navigatable spectral identifier.
#
# The TOP layer of Alex's 2026-06-06 three-layer recognition (see
# shards/glass.mirror's header and docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md
# §1B). Bottom (`splinter`, oid-addressed atom) and top (`spectral_uuid`,
# the spectral identity) meet in the middle at `shard` — the
# spectral_uuid-addressed settled composition. This shard declares the
# top layer at the substrate altitude so the middle layer's `id` slot in
# shards/glass.mirror can tighten from `oid` to `spectral_uuid` and the
# mosaic-as-type-system §4 Hilbert-space construction stops being a
# Rust-only fact.
#
# === The 128-bit layout, golden-ratio split ===
#
# Per prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs and
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] §3:
#
#   128 bits, golden-ratio split (≈1/φ²):
#     48 bits ACTIVE  — quantized SpectralCoordinate<5>; leading;
#                       graph-navigable. Carries the local Laplacian
#                       neighbourhood structure within a shard's
#                       splinter OID graph.
#     80 bits DARK    — BLAKE3-truncated content hash; trailing;
#                       identity. The settled splinter set's
#                       content-address prefix.
#
# Big-endian on the active portion: byte-wise sort over the leading
# bits IS lexicographic sort over the navigable coordinate. Range
# scans on the 48-bit space compose with byte-wise sort. The standard
# UUID hyphenated form (8-4-4-4-12) layers over the byte layout
# directly; hyphens land at positions 4, 6, 8, 10.
#
# === Monoid homomorphism w.r.t. shard merge ===
#
# Per docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §3:
#
#   spectral_uuid(merge(a, b)) = combine(spectral_uuid(a), spectral_uuid(b))
#
# Both halves compose homomorphically:
#   - dark 80 bits compose via the Merkle tree's content-address rule;
#   - active 48 bits compose via SpectralCoordinate's eigenvalue
#     addition law (to first order; weighted by content size).
#
# `empty` is the semilattice's bottom — λ₀ = 0 in spectral space,
# BLAKE3-of-empty in content space. The four monoid axioms (identity,
# associativity, commutativity, idempotency) hold by structural
# consequence of content-addressing + sorted-children, per
# reality-shard-as-crdt.md §1. The `requires monoidal(spectral_uuid)`
# declaration at the bottom is the substrate's compile-time witness.
#
# === Substrate placement ===
#
# Per the 2026-06-06 §9.9 OQ5 resolution in mosaic-as-type-system.md:
# `spectral_uuid` lives at @mirror/store as a sub-prism parallel to
# `@mirror/store/oid` (per shards/mirror/store.mirror:78-94). Both are
# content-addressed identity carriers at the store altitude; `oid`
# names the universal atomic content-address; `spectral_uuid` names
# the settled composition's graph-navigable address. The shard
# altitude (@glass) imports both.
#
# === Carrier shape ===
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: always newtype. `spectral_uuid` is a
# typed reference whose content IS its identity; following the
# @mirror/store/oid precedent (`type oid = ref`), the carrier is `ref`
# — the substrate's content-reference primitive. The 48/80 split is a
# property of the carrier, not a record field: the split is byte-stable
# at the realization layer (prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs) and is
# enforced structurally by the `combine` action's homomorphism and the
# active/dark accessor actions declared below. Lifting the split into
# a `{ active: u48, dark: u80 }` record at the substrate would require
# substrate scalar types (`@scalar/u48`, `@scalar/u80`) that do not yet
# exist; the ref-with-property-accessors form is the substrate-pull-
# correct shape today.
#
# === The deferred arithmetic ===
#
# Per reality-shard-as-crdt.md §11 OQ1, the quantized 48-bit
# arithmetic for `combine`'s active portion is still being pinned —
# it lands when SpectralCoordinate<5>'s eigenvalue composition rules
# quantize cleanly. The `combine` action below is declared with a `\`
# obligation block; the signature is well-defined (the monoid laws
# constrain it), the body is deferred to the same tick that pins the
# arithmetic. This is the standard substrate-pull discipline: declare
# what the substrate IS; defer the body to the consumer that needs it.
#
# Spec: docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §§2, 3, 11.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: glass.mirror (shard.id tightens to spectral_uuid),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the parent prism + oid sibling),
#                 mirror/mosaic.mirror (the algebra A whose D acts on
#                                       the spectral_uuid-indexed H).
# Reference: [[reference-void-document]] (λ₀ = 0 IS empty.active).
# Realisation: prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs (the carrier; this shard
#              names what the carrier IS at the substrate altitude).

# spectral_uuid is a sub-prism scoped to @mirror/store. The five-op
# block makes the sub-prism's identity explicit per the
# @mirror/store/oid precedent (shards/mirror/store.mirror:78-84).
glass @mirror/store/spectral_uuid {
  focus spectral_uuid
  project spectral_uuid
  split spectral_uuid
  shift spectral_uuid
  settle spectral_uuid
}

# === spectral_uuid — the carrier ===
#
# A typed reference. Content IS identity. Construction is by
# `from_parts(active, content_hash)` at the realization layer or by
# `combine` over an existing pair; equality is byte-equality of the
# resulting 16-byte reference. The 48/80 split is a structural
# property of the carrier enforced by the realization (per
# prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs's big-endian active-leading layout).
type spectral_uuid = ref

# === empty — the bottom of the semilattice ===
#
# Per docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §2: the canonical empty-
# shard address. λ₀ = 0 on the active 48 bits (the void axis per
# [[reference-void-document]]); BLAKE3 of empty input on the dark 80
# bits (the well-known constant `af1349b9f5f9a1a6a040`). Stable
# across all BLAKE3 implementations; byte-stable in the carrier.
#
# `fixed` per boot/std/mirror/glass/ast/shape/fixed.mirror: a fully
# settled crystal, content-addressed on declaration, no holes, no
# inference. The OID of this binding IS `empty`'s identity at the
# substrate altitude. The realization layer (prism/core/src/
# spectral_uuid.rs::EMPTY) is the byte-stable carrier; this
# declaration names the substrate-altitude fixed point.
fixed empty = spectral_uuid

# === active — the navigable 48 bits ===
#
# Project the navigable coordinate out of a spectral_uuid. The
# quantized SpectralCoordinate<5> — the local Laplacian neighbourhood
# encoding within a shard's splinter OID graph. Range scans on the
# active portion compose with byte-wise sort (the big-endian layout
# is what makes this work). Body deferred to the realization layer.
active(u: spectral_uuid) -> ref { \ }

# === dark — the identity 80 bits ===
#
# Project the content-hash prefix out of a spectral_uuid. The
# BLAKE3-truncated content hash — the splinter set's identity
# component. Two spectral_uuids with identical dark portions are
# composed from byte-equal splinter sets. Body deferred to the
# realization layer.
dark(u: spectral_uuid) -> ref { \ }

# === combine — the monoid homomorphism ===
#
# Per docs/specs/reality-shard-as-crdt.md §3:
#
#   spectral_uuid(merge(a, b)) = combine(spectral_uuid(a),
#                                        spectral_uuid(b))
#
# The active 48 bits compose via SpectralCoordinate's eigenvalue
# addition law (to first order; the spectral position of a union of
# content is the sum of the constituent positions weighted by content
# size). The dark 80 bits compose via the Merkle tree's existing
# content-address rule.
#
# Monoid laws (encoded by `requires monoidal(spectral_uuid)` below):
#
#   identity:        combine(empty, a) == a == combine(a, empty)
#   associativity:   combine(combine(a, b), c)
#                       == combine(a, combine(b, c))
#   commutativity:   combine(a, b) == combine(b, a)   (per §1: from
#                                                    sorted children)
#   idempotency:     combine(a, a) == a               (per §1: from
#                                                    content-address)
#
# The signature is well-defined; the body is deferred per the spec's
# §11 OQ1 — the quantized 48-bit arithmetic lands when
# SpectralCoordinate<5>'s eigenvalue composition rules quantize
# cleanly. Until then, the realization layer's `from_parts` re-derives
# the identifier from fresh inputs and `empty` carries the
# bottom-element semantics.
combine(a: spectral_uuid, b: spectral_uuid) -> spectral_uuid { \ }

# === properties: the math made load-bearing ===
#
# content_addressed(spectral_uuid) : identity IS the content hash.
#                                    Foundational; the substrate's
#                                    monoid structure rests on it.
#                                    Two spectral_uuids with byte-
#                                    equal carriers ARE the same
#                                    spectral_uuid.
#
# monoidal(spectral_uuid)          : combine + empty form a monoid.
#                                    Identity, associativity per
#                                    @epistemologic/property/laws/
#                                    monoidal. Commutativity +
#                                    idempotency follow from the
#                                    semilattice structure
#                                    (reality-shard-as-crdt.md §1)
#                                    — captured in the docstring;
#                                    the substrate-altitude property
#                                    declaration uses the existing
#                                    `monoidal` carrier (the parked
#                                    `identity_for` / `commutative` /
#                                    `idempotent` extensions per
#                                    reality-shard-as-crdt.md §10
#                                    tick 3 are not yet declared,
#                                    and per the discipline land
#                                    when their first consumer
#                                    surfaces).
requires content_addressed(spectral_uuid)
requires monoidal(spectral_uuid)

out @mirror/store/spectral_uuid
out spectral_uuid
out empty
out active
out dark
out combine
